WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.680
The Hammock Sea!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.660
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:42.230
Thank you, too.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.450
Tomorrow's your day off, so enjoy it.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.120
I will.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.300
It's a bit chilly lately.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.700
It has been.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.210
When I get home, I'm going to 
take a nice, hot bath and relax.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.550
Sounds good.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.920
Well, then good night.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.890
Yes. Good night.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.480
I love baths, too.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.870
Ice baths are the best!

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.860
This may be a little cramped.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.170
I'd like to have more room.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.230
Oh.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.820
Hey.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.400
How many sardines were in that soba?

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.230
Yes... There were eight sardines and...

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.100
Nine, ten, eleven...

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.650
What's wrong, Mr. Penguin?

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.770
Oh, it's you, Panda.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:04.070
Why are you mumbling to yourself?

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.110
Are you talking nonsense again?

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.690
Don't compare me to you!

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:12.820
I was just performing a 
story called "Sardine Soba."

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.060
Won't your mom get mad at you for eating

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.130
and walking at the same time?

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.550
I'm not eating!

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.800
This is comedic story-telling...

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:27.560
Mr. Penguin. If you walk 
around with your eyes closed,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.770
you might end up in someone else's house.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.830
No, I won't.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.460
Not to mention my eyes are wide open.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.380
What? I can't see them at all.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.280
Well, we can't really 
see your eyes, either.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.490
Call them cute and round.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.490
Or rather, what are you doing here?

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.080
This is my house.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.870
Did you need something, Mr. Penguin?

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.950
I'm sorry.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.850
Polar Bear's Café

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.880
It's gotten cold.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.400
It has.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.260
Continuing what we were 
talking about earlier,

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.860
but I'm thinking about doing some 
comedic storytelling at a party.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.490
It might get cold at the party, too.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.740
We don't need the rare 
witty comment from you.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:28.600
Not to mention, how do 
you know it'll be dull?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.230
You don't think it might 
actually be super funny?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:32.850
I doubt that.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.750
You're the only one that thinks that.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:38.710
Then do you want to have 
someone listen to it?

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.540
Good idea.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.670
Okay, then listen to this, Panda.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:47.830
Well, let's start off with 
another slightly idiotic tale...

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:48.810
Nah.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.140
Hey, listen!

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.560
What's wrong?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.570
Closed

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.060
It says they're closed.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:06.120
Polar Bear doesn't hesitate 
to close up, does he?

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.280
You want Polar Bear to listen?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:16.250
Yeah. I thought we'd have him 
listen to your boring stories.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.630
They aren't boring! They're hilarious!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.590
Huh?

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.480
I wonder what Polar Bear's 
doing in the yard.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.930
He's got a big cloth.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.790
Maybe he's running away? 
We've got to stop him!

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.890
He's not you, you know.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.060
Then maybe he's a thief?

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.850
What's he going to steal 
from his own place?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.670
Oh, I know!

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:50.130
He must be Santa!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.800
What he's holding is his bag of presents!

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:02.140
Christmas came and went a long time ago!

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.840
There must be a present for me in there!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.380
Hey, wait! Panda?!

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:11.810
Maybe right here...

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:15.480
Yes. The distance between 
these trees is about perfect.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.490
I wonder what's in here.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.360
Hey, it's empty.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.730
Oh, Panda and Mr. Penguin.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:27.510
Hey.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:29.660
Where's my present?

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.530
What? A present?

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.670
Yeah! This is a bag of presents, right?

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.830
Oh, this is for relaxing.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.290
Relaxing?

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.820
Yeah, watch.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.140
I'm going to put a cushion on 
the tree and then tie this end.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:57.970
And then...

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.860
Oh! A hammock!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:07.680
Yup.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:12.060
Hey, Polar Bear, could I get in?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:12.870
Sure.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.830
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.830
You can get in, too, Mr. Penguin.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.750
Thanks!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:26.260
Mr. Penguin, if you want, 
you can go ahead...

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:27.420
Really?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:30.560
...and watch me get in.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.110
Really? What is this?

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.600
It's big, so we can in together.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:39.180
I see!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.060
Yay!

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.770
It's swaying!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.840
This is fun!

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.440
Oh, if it sways too much...

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.240
We fell out...

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.910
You're heavy, Panda!

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.080
The way you lay in a hammock is...

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.630
Like this.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:11.090
First, you sit in the center 
carefully, and then roll back.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.670
If you lay sideways or at an angle,

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:16.100
it's harder to slip out and is ideal.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.190
You're right!

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:21.430
It would've been nice if 
you had told us that earlier.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:28.630
Thanks for waiting.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.200
It's delicious.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.050
Having coffee like this isn't bad at all.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:37.320
Right?

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.430
This is nice.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:50.850
Sure is.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.120
This is relaxing.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:10.620
By the way, Mr. Penguin, 
why did we come here again?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.750
Why <i>did</i> you come here?

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.440
Oh, that's right.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.360
I'm practicing my comedic storytelling 
for the next party and...

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.310
I think it wasn't anything important.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.210
What?!

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:25.070
I see. So, it wasn't important.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.250
It does matter!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:37.340
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.650
The way the hammock is swaying,

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.820
I feel like I'm floating in the ocean.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:19.010
It reminds me of when I was swimming 
around in the arctic ocean.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:24.890
Now I'll enjoy that feeling from here.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:35.820
Closed

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:39.470
It's so cold!

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.740
It snowed quite a bit today.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.590
S-Something very large is in the yard!

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.230
Oh, good morning, Miss Sasako.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:07.470
Mr. Polar Bear?

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.480
It's wonderfully chilly this morning.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.670
I slept so well.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:23.780
Mr. Polar Bear...

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:27.020
Nothing less from someone 
from the Arctic...

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.590
Panda Mama's Gardening.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.480
Hello?

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:03.160
Oh, Grizzly? It's Polar Bear.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:06.160
You again?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.290
Grizzly,

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:11.900
should I grill the New Year's rice cakes

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:13.580
or make them into ozouni soup?

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:17.540
Why are you asking me?

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:21.720
I told you, I'm hibernating, damn it!

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.090
I can't decide between the two

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:27.370
and I've been losing sleep over this.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:29.720
What do you think I should do?

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.400
Shut up and let me sleep!

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.860
Panda

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.740
Get up. It's already noon.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.790
Let me sleep just a little longer...

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.760
That's enough.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:57.230
How long do you have to 
sleep to be satisfied?

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.570
Anytime I'm not awake.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:05.660
Goodness. You do nothing but sleep.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:07.180
Do you plan on hibernating?

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:12.680
Mom, bears don't call it hibernating.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.890
They call it staying in 
for the winter.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.460
Oh, really?

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.220
Yup.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:23.730
They say that pandas can't 
stay indoors for the winter,

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:26.860
but I'll do my best to try!

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:30.780
Okay, wake me up in the spring.

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:39.930
Don't suck me up!

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:43.800
Well, then...

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:47.760
Since I'm done with the 
cleaning for now...

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.670
I'll take a moment

00:13:57.510 --> 00:13:59.200
to enjoy myself.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:03.110
Oh, it's mom.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.180
She's cultivating the yard again.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:08.710
She sure likes that.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:09.810
Oh, my.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.790
Call it "gardening."

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:23.280
Lately, it's not just flowers and trees,

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:27.680
but I've started growing vegetables, too.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.660
It's nice when a lot of 
vegetables grow

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.600
because we'll have so 
much more to eat.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.390
The flowers and the vegetable 
garden keep me rather busy.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.160
Th-The tulip buds are gone!

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:55.500
How...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.620
Oh, those were tulips?

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:03.340
I thought they were green 
onions and I ate them.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.460
You ate them?!

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.640
No wonder they didn't 
taste like green onions.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.760
The green onions are over there!

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:15.180
Oh, you're right.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.560
H-How could this happen?

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:21.350
Cute little flowers should 
have bloomed in the spring.

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.620
How could you?!

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.450
And I wanted to make a garden 
like Ms. Tasha Panda.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:38.200
Live a Mellow, 
Relaxing Life

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.330
With a garden like this,

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:43.620
how will I ever face Ms. Tasha Panda?

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.090
Oh, that foolish child...

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:52.300
Five, six, seven...

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:57.810
Hey, how many sardines 
were in that soba?

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.840
There were four.

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.820
Hey, there's less.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:02.670
One...

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:08.230
Ack! Hey! Don't butt in at 
the best part, Polar Bear!

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.190
Sorry about that.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.020
Jeez. Were you even listening?

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:17.120
Come to think of it, neither of 
you even laughed once, did you?

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:21.780
Why?

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:23.830
Well...

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.250
Um...

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.230
I don't think you know where 
you're supposed to laugh.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.980
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.950
This is the tenth time, but I'm 
starting from the top again.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.830
Huh? Wait, you don't...

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.680
Oh, hello, Panda. Welcome.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.440
What's the matter? You seem down.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:52.610
How about I cheer you up with 
one of my comedic stories?

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.650
Maybe we should skip that.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:57.970
Why?!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.400
Well, you see...

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:04.760
I accidentally ate my mom's tulips because

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:07.250
I thought they were green onions.

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:09.250
What?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:13.030
I'm guessing that your mom 
was a little mad about that.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:16.790
Yeah... that's why I ran away to here.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:19.950
You eat anything, don't you?

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:23.140
So, I was wondering, Polar Bear...

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:24.630
Yes?

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:27.860
Could you spare some of your flowers?

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.690
What kind of tulips did you eat?

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.070
I already ate them, so I have no idea.

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:39.780
Oh, I see.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.750
How about picking out some 
flowers that your mom will like?

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.970
Oh, good idea.

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:50.460
But I wonder what kind 
of flowers she'll like.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:58.430
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:01.970
Hello.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.140
Welcome, Panda!

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.150
What can I get you today?

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:08.080
Look! I've got bamboo grass, too!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.310
It's scrumptious!

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.450
I don't need anything from you, Rin Rin.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.490
Oh, I see...

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:17.150
Don't be like that, Panda.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.450
You came here because 
you need somethig, right?

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.380
What's wrong?

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:31.940
I see...

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:34.680
So I brought him here

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:38.330
so you could maybe help 
us pick out some flowers

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:40.140
that might cheer his mom up.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:44.970
You garden at home, too, right?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:49.100
So do you know something
 my mom would like?

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:53.180
I might know...

00:18:53.670 --> 00:19:00.570
But would it be enough to just 
plant flowers your mom may like?

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.420
Well, you've got a point.

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:15.490
I know!

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.430
Panda

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.850
Mom.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:27.460
What is it?

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.160
I'm really sorry

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:37.280
for eating your tulips yesterday.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.230
Oh.

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:42.390
I planted some other flowers,

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.240
so please forgive me.

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:49.590
Oh, all right. Show them to me.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:57.150
He should be showing her the 
flowers right about now.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:20:00.130
I hope she likes them.

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:05.270
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:07.870
I'd love to hear the results soon.

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:09.450
Oh, I know.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.980
While we're waiting for Panda's results,

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.480
I'll do some of my comedic storytelling.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:15.930
Comedic storytelling?

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:17.570
Again?

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:19.440
All right, here we go.

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.560
The title is Sardine Soba.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:25.210
One night, a soba stand 
owner was setting up,

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:28.540
when a customer called out, 
"Hey, soba stand owner..."

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.100
And that's all from me...

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:38.680
Hey! I just started, Polar Bear!

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:41.690
Never mind. Can I get 
another café mocha?

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:42.840
Sure.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:45.980
Over here.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:04.240
Oh, some wild chrysanthemums 
and purples pansies?

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.460
Quite a stoic arrangement.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.420
Climb up here, Mom.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.630
What is it?

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.840
Oh my...

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:37.520
I-It's my face!

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:47.660
<i>I wonder... if she likes them...</i>

00:22:00.730 --> 00:22:04.230
<i>It didn't end up like Ms. Tasha Panda's,</i>

00:22:08.710 --> 00:22:12.930
<i>but it's become my very 
own one-of-a-kind garden.</i>

00:22:17.390 --> 00:22:18.640
Thank you.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.920
Next Time

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.770
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:00.980
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.980 --> 00:24:04.260
I'll give you one minute, 
so show me everything you've got.

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:06.520
I'd rather not give that a try.

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:09.740
I guess everything you have 
doesn't take a whole minute...

00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:11.760
Is that what I was hinting at?

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:13.490
Next week's Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:13.490 --> 00:24:15.480
Butting right in I see, Miss Sasako...

00:24:15.480 --> 00:24:17.180
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:19.100
Next week's Tottoko Polar Bear's Café

00:24:19.100 --> 00:24:20.310
Let's leave out "Tottoko."

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:21.280
On Polar Bear Eleven—

00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:22.090
End!

00:24:22.040 --> 00:24:23.500
Scattering Beans with Everyone
The Café in the Afternoon

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:23.500
Enjoy!
